        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Furnishing fabric 'Leaf and Crown' of silk twill satin, made by Daniel Keith & Co., Spitalfields, London, ca. 1867"@en , "Furnishing fabric of silk twill satin. The pattern, in pale yellow twill on a fuchsia pink satin ground, is of a small stylised crown that is enclosed in a roundel of four leaves that form parts of large trefoils on this stems springing from crowns in half-drop repeat to left and right. Three smaller stylised blossoms, also springing from the crowns, fill the arched spaces beneath the leaves. One end of the silk has a plain 0.75 inch."@en ;
